  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the children as the subject of the hateful message",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the children, as the text 'they have no where to live' and 'makes special camp spots just for them' explicitly attributes these conditions to the children depicted. The user is not directly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the entire meme functions as a projection of the user's perspective onto the children as the target of the antisemitic stereotype. The user is implicitly positioned as the one who understands or is conveying this hateful message, thereby projecting themselves onto the children as the 'they' in the text.",
